    grammarFocus: 'Targets: It tells us that … / It shows that … + present simple for a lesson · said to + person · told + person/thing + to + base verb · place and time words (very close behind, entered, midway, In the end, no one).\nNotice (Activity 1): “It tells us that no one can own another person. It shows that only Allah has power over us.” Ask: “Is this a new event, the king’s words or a lesson? Why tells and shows, not told and showed?”\nBuild (Activities 2–3): fix “said his soldiers” and “told the sea open”, then match very close behind, entered, midway, In the end and no one with their meanings.\nLikely errors: *The king said his soldiers · *told the sea open · *told to the sea · *It told us that (past for a lesson) · *No one can owns.\nUse (Activity 4): a short everyday story and its lesson (In the end, … . It tells us that … . It shows that …).',
